/Title (Visual reasoning: The yellow contour is placed within the LV cavity and follows the inner cavity edge from the basal region toward the apex. The filled area represents the cavity rather than the outer myocardial boundary. The basal closure is drawn between the two basal endpoints, consistent with the guideline's description of closing the contour at the mitral-valve level.)
